{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{confix|hyper|opia}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} A disorder of the vision where the eye focusses images behind the [[retina]] instead of on it, so that distant objects can be seen better than near objects.

====Synonyms====
* [[farsightedness]]
* [[hypermetropia]]
* [[hypermetropy]]

====Derived terms====
* [[hyperope]]
* [[hyperopic]]

====See also====
* [[astigmatism]]
* [[emmetropia]] 
* [[presbyopia]]
* [[myopia]]

